{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/fred2005-formal-groups/blocks/def-non-commutative-formal-group","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:non-commutative-formal-group","kind":"definition","title":"Non-commutative formal group","uses":["papers/fred2005-formal-groups/blocks/def-commutative-formal-group"],"cites":["references/fred2005"],"tags":["formal-group","non-commutative","distribution-algebra"],"leanRef":"fred2005:Fred2005.NoncommutativeFormalGroup","text":"non-commutative-formal-group.md","leanSource":"folio/fred2005-formal-groups/formal-groups-chapter/non-commutative-formal-group.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:non-commutative-formal-group\"></a><p>A <strong>non-commutative formal group</strong> is the output of the integration\ntheorem.  It is a formal group <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G</code> over <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{Z}_p</code> whose\ndistribution algebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Dist}(G)</code> carries:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A (generally non-commutative) multiplication <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mu</code>.</li>\n<li>A comultiplication <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta</code> satisfying <strong>strong multiplicativity</strong>:\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta(xy) = \\Delta(x) \\cdot \\Delta(y)</code> component-wise.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The base <a href=\"#def:commutative-formal-group\">commutative formal group</a>\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H / \\mathbb{F}_p</code> is recovered by reduction modulo <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p</code>.</p>\n<p>Reference: <span class=\"cite\" data-keys=\"fred2005\">[fred2005]</span>, Main Theorem.</p>\n","source":"folio/fred2005-formal-groups/formal-groups-chapter/non-commutative-formal-group.md","heading":"Definition","number":"1.3.1"}
